 \\\\  & =-{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }5(\\lambda +n){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n}, \\\\ (x+3)y & =(x+3){\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n+1}+{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }3{a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the first sum of the $y$ term, we change the index of the summation by writing $m=n+1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n(x+3)y={\\sum }_{m=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{m-1}{x}^{\\lambda +m}+{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }3{a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n}.\n$$\n\nThen, replacing $m$ with $n$ (since it does not matter which letter we use) and isolating the $n=0$ term gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+3)y & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n-1}{x}^{\\lambda +n}+{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }3{a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n-1}{x}^{\\lambda +n}+3{a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda }+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }3{a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, isolating the $n=0$ terms for the other terms in the ODE, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}{y}^{″} & =4({\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda ){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda }+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }4((\\lambda +n)^{2}-(\\lambda +n)){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n}, \\\\ -5x{y}^{′} & =-5\\lambda {a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda }-{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }5(\\lambda +n){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: Consolidate all the series into a single series that is equal to $0.$\n\nCollecting the terms for $n=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4({\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda ){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda }-5\\lambda {a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda }+3{a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda } & = \\\\ (4{\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda -5\\lambda +3){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda } & = \\\\ (4{\\lambda }^{2}-9\\lambda +3){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda } & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, collecting terms for $n\\ge 1,$ we obtain an infinite series of the form\n${x}^{\\lambda }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}(\\lambda ){x}^{n},$\nfor some ${b}_{n}(\\lambda ),$ $n\\ge 1.$\nTherefore, substituting into the homogeneous ODE, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4{\\lambda }^{2}-9\\lambda +3){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda }+{x}^{\\lambda }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}(\\lambda ){x}^{n} & =0 \\\\ (4{\\lambda }^{2}-9\\lambda +3){a}_{0}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}(\\lambda ){x}^{n} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 5**:  Set the coefficients of the series equal to $0.$\n\nSetting the coefficient of the $n=0$ term equal to $0$ with arbitrary ${a}_{0}\\ne 0,$ we obtain the indicial equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4{\\lambda }^{2}-9\\lambda +3){a}_{0} & =0 \\\\ 4{\\lambda }^{2}-9\\lambda +3 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535663 true] [17592186359947 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359948 13194139535663 true] [17592186359947 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359949 13194139535663 true] [17592186359947 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359950 13194139535663 true] [17592186359947 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359951 13194139535663 true] [17592186359947 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359952 13194139535663 true] [17592186359947 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535663 true] [17592186359947 1041 "selection" 13194139535663 true] [17592186359947 1104 #edb/ref 17592186359948 13194139535663 true] [17592186359947 1110 #uuid "bf98d2dd-a291-5ddf-aecf-f5b17b7d58a2" 13194139535663 true] [17592186359948 1034 "4{\\lambda }^{2}-9\\lambda +3=0" 13194139535663 true] [17592186359948 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535663 true] [17592186359948 1111 #uuid "7bcd87ec-7a52-522f-8f5d-53562c1fc36e" 13194139535663 true] [17592186359949 1034 "4{\\lambda }^{2}-8\\lambda +3=0" 13194139535663 true] [17592186359949 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535663 true] [17592186359949 1111 #uuid "4a1be3de-d75a-506b-93ed-db4b1ea9dffd" 13194139535663 true] [17592186359950 1034 "4{\\lambda }^{2}+9\\lambda +3=0" 13194139535663 true] [17592186359950 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535663 true] [17592186359950 1111 #uuid "81977c79-4114-5a54-b113-8b4dea52eb18" 13194139535663 true] [17592186359951 1034 "{\\lambda }^{2}-9\\lambda +3=0" 13194139535663 true] [17592186359951 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139