and\n\n- a recurrence formula from the coefficients of the $n\\ge 1$ terms.\n\nWe are given the three terms of the ODE as power series with the $n=0$ term isolated in each.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{2}{y}^{″} & =6({\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda ){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda }+6{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }((\\lambda +n)^{2}-(\\lambda +n)){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n}, \\\\ x(6x+1){y}^{′} & =\\lambda {a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda }+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }[6(\\lambda +n-1){a}_{n-1}+(\\lambda +n){a}_{n}]{x}^{\\lambda +n}, \\\\ y & ={a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda }+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we continue from this point.\n\n**Step 1**: Consolidate all the series into a single series that is equal to $0.$\n\nCollecting the terms for $n=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6({\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda ){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda }+\\lambda {a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda }+{a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda } & = \\\\ (6{\\lambda }^{2}-6\\lambda +\\lambda +1){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda } & = \\\\ (6{\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda +1){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda } & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, collecting terms for $n\\ge 1,$ we obtain an infinite series of the form\n${x}^{\\lambda }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}(\\lambda ){x}^{n},$\nfor some ${b}_{n}(\\lambda ),$ $n\\ge 1.$\nTherefore, substituting into the homogeneous ODE, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(6{\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda +1){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda }+{x}^{\\lambda }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}(\\lambda ){x}^{n} & =0 \\\\ (6{\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda +1){a}_{0}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}(\\lambda ){x}^{n} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**:  Set the coefficients of the series equal to $0.$\n\nSetting the coefficient of the $n=0$ term equal to $0$ with arbitrary ${a}_{0}\\ne 0,$ we obtain the indicial equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(6{\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda +1){a}_{0} & =0 \\\\ 6{\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda +1 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can determine a solution.\nSolving the indicial equation for the roots, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda +1 & =0 \\\\ (3\\lambda -1)(2\\lambda -1) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =\\frac{1}{3},\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the two Frobenius series solutions are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}(x)={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n+1/3}\\,\\text{and}\\,{y}_{2}(x)={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n+1/2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere the constants ${a}_{n}$ are to be determined separately in each of the two cases.\n\nOf the given options, the correct answer is\n$y(x)={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n+1/2}.$" 13194139535663 true] [17592186359982 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359983 13194139535663 true] [17592186359982 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359984 13194139535663 true] [17592186359982 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359985 13194139535663 true] [17592186359982 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359986 13194139535663 true] [17592186359982 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359987 13194139535663 true] [17592186359982 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535663 true] [17592186359982 1041 "selection" 13194139535663 true] [17592186359982 1104 #edb/ref 17592186359987 13194139535663 true] [17592186359982 1110 #uuid "df64f0b3-49af-552b-9739-e8ef5776a0b0" 13194139535663 true] [17592186359983 1034 "y(x)={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1/2}" 13194139535663 true] [17592186359983 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535663 true] [17592186359983 1111 #uuid "79d15c46-3335-54d1-9011-5f47a699e758" 13194139535663 true] [17592186359984 1034 "y(x)={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n/2}" 13194139535663 true] [17592186359984 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535663 true] [17592186359984 1111 #uuid "830deb66-f6db-5bfb-b439-cddd5593b53c" 13194139535663 true] [17592186359985 1034 "y(x)={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1/3}" 13194139535663 true] [17592186359985 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535663 true] [17592186359985 1111 #uuid "b5e4a637-e56b-5c40-9731-d526e6b1b535" 13194139535663 true] [17592186359986 1034 "y(x)={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n+2/3}" 13194139535663 